{
  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "game": "elvis",
  "notes": "Boot elvis (5.00) with four balls on trough switches 11-14 and the stacking opto 15 at 0, with built-in mechanisms off (--handle-mechanics 0). Walk the Portals service menu with the Black ENTER button (public 0): Portals, MAIN MENU (DIAG), DIAGNOSTICS MENU (SW), SWITCH TEST MENU (TEST), and enter the Switch Test, which prints after each closure the name, the drive and return wire colours and the number the ROM holds for that switch. Close every matrix address 1-64 once and read the display 0.7 s and 1.5 s after the closure; an address closed at boot is first opened and is left closed again afterwards. That includes 33: LibPinMAME's elvis.c sets 33 to 1 on the boot write to the stepper phases 25-28 and writes it again only on a later nonzero phase write, which this run never sees after boot, so the 33 edges in the Switch Test are the scenario's own.",
